course: dictionary
lesson: 12406
title: Customary: the usual way
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Customary is a formal word that means usual. It describes what normally happens, or what people have always done as a tradition. «It is customary to shake hands when you meet someone new.» That means people usually do this, because it is the custom.
explain: Writers also use it in stories. «He gave his customary smile.» Here customary means his usual smile, the one he always gives. To check, swap in usual or normal: «He gave his usual smile» still makes sense.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like tradition, always or every year often show that something is customary. «On New Year's Day, the family eats their customary soup» tells you it is an old habit they repeat each year.
fact: Customary means usual, normal, or traditional.
fact: Customary is a formal word, so you will often see it in books, history lessons and official writing.
fact: The phrases «it is customary to» and «as is customary» mean it is the usual thing to do.
fact: In everyday talk, people usually say «usual» or «normal» instead of customary.
fact: «With his customary smile» means with his usual smile.
exercise: «With her customary smile, Mum waved goodbye at the gate.» What does customary mean here? | Angry | Sleepy | Lost | *Usual
exercise: Which word could replace customary in «It is customary to take off your shoes at the door»? | Loud | Strange | Expensive | *Usual
exercise: «They followed the customary way of greeting the king.» What does customary suggest? | A long trip across the sea | A new game they invented today | *A tradition people have always followed | A secret plan
test: The phrase «it is customary to» means it is | the hardest thing to do | the cheapest thing to do | the last thing to do | *the usual thing to do
test: Which word is the best swap for customary in «her customary cup of tea»? | Hot | Strange | *Usual | Empty
exam: Mia says, «Customary means strange.» Who is right? | *Mia is wrong, because it means usual | Nobody, the word has no meaning | Mia, because it means loud | Mia, because it means strange
